<title>USA: STM Wireless sells system to Chinese paper.</title>
<headline>STM Wireless sells system to Chinese paper.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>STM Wireless Inc said on Friday it sold one of its DAMA 10000 satellite networks to the Economic Daily newspaper in China.</p>
<p>Financial details were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The network, which will have its control center based in Beijing, will be used for remote publishing and for central database inquires from offices and reporter stations around China.</p>
<p>The Economic Daily is supervised by the State Department of China. It broadcasts the nation's economic news and policies, and it has a circulation of over 800,000 copies.</p>
</text>
